Any `RunHooks` callback the SDK adds later (like `on_llm_start`/`on_llm_end` were) resolves to the inherited no-op here, so the user's override is silently dropped once they upgrade the SDK. `test_run_hooks_implement_sdk_callbacks` only catches it for the tested version. Maybe forward everything not overridden:

```python
    def __getattribute__(self, name: str) -> Any:
        if name.startswith("on_") and name not in GenAIRunHooks.__dict__:
            return getattr(object.__getattribute__(self, "_hooks"), name)
        return object.__getattribute__(self, name)
```
